---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'Survival Math in Diablo IV – Toughness & EHP Guide';
const description =
  'Survival math for Diablo IV: effective HP, the armor curve, why one-shots are a budget problem, and how much toughness endgame content actually demands.';
const updated = SITE.lastVerified;
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Guides' }, { name: 'Survival Math' }]}
  schema={[{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'Survival math for Diablo IV',
    datePublished: '2026-10-08',
    dateModified: updated,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.brand },
  }]}
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Survival math</h1>
    <div class="h1-bar"></div>
    <p class="lede">
      Damage gets the guides; deaths get the blame. But staying alive is its own arithmetic — EHP, armor
      curves, and a damage budget you can actually plan around.
    </p>
    <div class="microline"><span>By {SITE.brand}</span><span>Updated {updated}</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Quick answer</h2>
    <p>
      Convert life, armor and resistances into effective HP with the <a href="/toughness-calculator/">toughness
      calculator</a>, then size that number against the content: you want roughly 2–3× the raw damage of a
      typical elite swing before pushing higher Pit tiers.
    </p>

    <h2>EHP is the only fair comparison</h2>
    <p>
      "Should I take Life or armor?" is unanswerable in isolation — they multiply into the same currency:
      effective HP. Life is its own bucket; armor and resistances are mitigation buckets. As with damage,
      grow whichever multiplier is currently smaller.
    </p>

    <h2>Why you're getting one-shot</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><strong>Elite swings carry multipliers</strong> — your EHP floor is set against those, not trash hits.</li>
      <li><strong>Enemy level scales with content tier</strong> — armor's mitigation shrinks as you push; re-run the calculator with the real enemy level.</li>
      <li><strong>Resist caps exist</strong> — stacking past the cap buys nothing [VERIFY current caps per season].</li>
      <li><strong>Some mechanics partially bypass mitigation</strong> — no EHP fixes those; movement does.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>The toughness budget</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Farming tier:</strong> survive comfortably, drop toughness for damage.</li>
      <li><strong>Push tier:</strong> 2–3× elite-swing EHP, or accept that death timers cost more than the stats would.</li>
      <li><strong>Trade deliberately:</strong> every toughness affix is damage not taken — use the <a href="/damage-calculator/">damage calculator</a> to price the trade instead of guessing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">Armor curve constants shift between seasons — the model's K is editable and flagged [VERIFY]. <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
